    <briefdescription>
<para>Data queries for one series: nearest data points, brackets, region statistics, and index pages. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Available as <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1PlotSeries_1addb81876423cd48343592cfce8c19d5b" kindref="member">PlotSeries::inspection</ref></computeroutput>. Call it on the series&apos; thread. Pixel arguments are series-local logical pixels; regions are inclusive data-space limits, where an infinite limit leaves that side unbounded and reversed limits are swapped.</para>
<para>Queries cover every stored data point, also outside the viewport, and match data points rather than the line segments between them. Invalid data points never match, and equal distances resolve to the highest index. Statistics are data-point-weighted and use the original Y values.</para>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1LineCurve" kindref="compound">LineCurve</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1PointCloud" kindref="compound">PointCloud</ref></computeroutput> answer every query. Series whose X or Y values are finite and non-decreasing are searched in place, need no preparation, and stay queryable while records are appended; queries along one axis, such as <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1SeriesInspection_1aef688dea1ecf19a548adab732b2fd35e" kindref="member">nearestByX()</ref></computeroutput>, need that order along their own axis. Other series of up to 20,000 records are scanned per query. Larger ones are indexed on a worker thread first; until then queries return <computeroutput>Inspection.Preparing</computeroutput>. Requesting an index copies the series&apos; buffer once on the calling thread, the index takes about 40 MB per million valid data points, and any data change discards it. Other series types expose native records through <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1SeriesInspection_1aadbb75d7ac32131dcc24a739cfe2b71c" kindref="member">recordAt()</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1SeriesInspection_1a307a83285fc1a108a34eba585beb814d" kindref="member">recordAtPosition()</ref></computeroutput> only; <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1HeatmapSeries" kindref="compound">HeatmapSeries</ref></computeroutput> also answers <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1SeriesInspection_1adac020ef11a2a3fce54790fe2e9c5146" kindref="member">dataPointAtPosition()</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1PlotInspector" kindref="compound">PlotInspector</ref>, <ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1SelectionTool" kindref="compound">SelectionTool</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
